#### 5.1.4 \(N_{part}\) dependence of near-side yields

The near-side jet-like yield is presented as a function of number of participant nucleons (\(N_{part}\)) in Fig. 5.13 (for \(4<p_{T}^{trig}<6\) GeV/c) and Fig. 5.14 (for \(6<p_{T}^{trig}<10\) GeV/c). As already mentioned, it can be easily seen that the two analysis methods give consistent results. The Cu+Cu and Au+Au near-side associated yields are consistent within errors for similar \(N_{part}\). The near side yields in heavy ion collisions show no centrality dependence and within errors agree with those in d+Au, as seen also in previous studies of Au+Au collisions [39]. The independence of the near-side associated yields on centrality indicates that high-\(p_{T}\) trigger particles select partons for which fragmentation is largely unmodified by the presence of the medium.

